                <pb facs="0194" n="86" xml:id="pg86"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-25"><hi rendition="#italic">December 25, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 27.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson communicates a notice sent by the insurgents to the Italian admiral
                    of their intention to bombard should they not receive recognition as
                    belligerents; he observes that the engagements with the insurgents have not been
                    enforced by the naval commanding officers and reports that a very perceptible
                    change of feeling in favor of the Government has been created by the
                    proclamation in which Da Gama favors the restoration of the Empire.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
